## Context

Author request: "Add tickets to test what they test, we want at least as good
guarantees." This is a test-parity work train, not a claim of present parity or
authorization to replace ratified scheduling policy.

Baseline inspected: zotero/zotero#6012 head
19e79625b1c6fbbdd75367aa85b62d5a7080d7f6, read 2026-09-08.
Pinned suites:
- https://github.com/zotero/zotero/blob/19e79625b1c6fbbdd75367aa85b62d5a7080d7f6/test/tests/embeddingsTest.js
- https://github.com/zotero/zotero/blob/19e79625b1c6fbbdd75367aa85b62d5a7080d7f6/test/tests/sdtTest.js

Read before filing: plugins/sdt-sitter/bootstrap.js and scheduler.js;
tests/sdt_sitter_scheduler.mjs and bootstrap tests; fork/src/features/search/
build.ts and embeddings.ts; SYNC.md upstream and Zotero core rows.
make upstream-catchup returned TOUCHED at zoteus 357ad1f, after UPSTREAM's
baseline: changes include attachment-read retry/preservation, shared index
metadata, code invalidation and explicit semantic-mode refusal tests. Inspect
those existing implementations and tests before proposing additions. This
ticket does not re-baseline historical evidence.

## Work and exit criteria

- [ ] Commit verification/6012-GUARANTEE-PARITY.md mapping each behavior asserted
      by the pinned suites to its purpose, owning SPEC requirement/design
      section, responsible component and exact local test/evidence path.
- [ ] Distinguish tested equivalent, missing test, observed failure, inherited
      native guarantee, deliberate design difference and inapplicable behavior.
      A mocked native success is not evidence for the inherited guarantee.
- [ ] Include chunk boundaries and source locations, auxiliary/reference
      handling, notes/annotations, stale previews, model identity and switching,
      embedding retries, concurrent requests, calibration, deletion and memory
      pressure, as well as extraction and scheduling.
- [ ] Read the pinned heads at source, not only their test suites. A guarantee
      no test asserts is invisible to a suite-driven matrix, and startup pacing
      is the found instance: `embeddings.js`'s `init()` waits 5 s before
      `startIndexing()` "so we don't compete with window setup", beside a 3 s
      `KICK_DELAY` debounce, and neither suite asserts either. Mark such rows
      source-read and say so where the evidence is a reading, not a run.
- [ ] Route sitter cases to 0755 and 0756; readiness to 0757. Route remaining
      consumer cases to existing tickets where possible, otherwise file bounded
      local test tickets after inspecting current fork/upstream code.
- [ ] Do not copy smallest-first ordering, numerical settings or fallback
      semantics over different ratified contracts. Record the user-visible
      guarantee and unresolved differences; any new design choice goes through
      DECISIONS.md and SPEC.md before implementation.
- [ ] Each applicable row has discriminating evidence or an open owning ticket.
      Open failures, unmeasured native behavior and skips preclude claiming
      parity for that row. Test counts alone never establish parity.
- [ ] 0755, 0756 and 0757 outcomes are reflected in the matrix; make check passes.

Reports are evidence; requirements and design numbers remain in SPEC.md.

## Existing pipeline work to reuse

The author's reminder prompted a branch-and-log read: fork branch
origin/conductor-integration contains the ledger, election, reconciliation,
extraction dispatcher/drain, pacing, activity and priority modules; seg/1 also
exists on origin/t0028-seg1. The checked-out fork alone hides this work.
Read 0568 and 0028's logs and those branches before claiming an absent module.
The existing continuation owners are 0565 (segmenter write-loop wiring), 0554
(bounded embed worker/client), 0575 (shared embedding service) and 0566
(runnable process assembly). Route relevant parity tests to those tickets;
do not create a duplicate chunk/embedding-sitter implementation train.
STATE.md's hold on the indexer/worker rewrite remains in force; auditing and
testing available modules does not authorize resuming that implementation.

Include the GPU/runtime boundary in the parity map: reuse
verification/BRIDGE-0496.md, 0491, 0493 and 0575. Verify actual device usability,
query/passage vector compatibility and endpoint failure behavior; #6012's
outbound passage endpoint is not its local query path. Do not infer GPU use
from an out-of-process engine or a configured device name, and do not count
the sitter's pack production as evidence that embedding used a GPU.
